  "unreadable": [],
  "notes": "Image is a FRONT/BACK edge-connector pin diagram without a board drawing. Front and back are recorded as separate connectors because the rows have different pin counts (34 front, 33 back) and a gap/key at different offsets. Labels use the IO number (GPIO name) since no silkscreen is distinguished; functions are the other boxes reading outward from the edge. Back pins 'D-'/'D+' are labeled with their GPIO names IO19/IO20 with D-/D+ as functions. MAX17048G fuel gauge (IO9/IO8/IO6) and ANT IO38 boxes are internal callouts, not edge pins, and were skipped."
